      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I understand the test. It verifies that `UnicodeEscaper.between()` with an inverted range (low=55296 > high=1166) returns `false` from `translate()` for the low boundary value. I'll improve the understandability with named constants, descriptive variable names, and a meaningful test method name.The improved test compiles successfully. The refactored `test4` now uses named constants (`HIGH_SURROGATE_START`, `CYRILLIC_CODE_POINT`), a descriptive method name (`test4_translateReturnsFalseWhenBetweenRangeIsInverted`), meaningful variable names (`escaperWithInvertedRange`, `output`, `wasEscaped`), and a comment explaining the inverted-range scenario — all while preserving the exact same method calls, arguments, and assertion as the original."
